selftext:
I love how she captured the many prototypes I went through. I haven't seen much content where different stages / experiments of a particular game in development were shown => decided it could be useful, or at least mildly entertaining for someone to see. 

Some curious bits from my experience:

\- it was extremely fun to make big iterations on the prototype through X hours, not X days, as it has taken me prior to AI-era; I tried many ideas I wouldn't ever have time for, normally;

\- I envisioned this game in 2D, but no matter which angles I approached it with (including isometry) it just didn't feel fun;

\- I tried 3D on GPT Sol Extra High... and it made a terrible job, the wobbly building in the vid is its result. Then for lolz I tried Luna Extra High Effort for a 3D from scratch and... it produced a fun, cohesive experience (result after some iterations can be seen as the last prototype);

\- none of these are one shot, each is crafted through careful iterations and exact development intent;

\- overall, I did have a lot of fun, though it has taken lots of time. As a result, I made corrections for my vision of the game, and where I could realistically take it next.

For all of these I used Codex, for 2D graphics GPT ImageGen (available thru codex), for 3D - code-made assets made by LLM itself.
